text:
sam: Observed weird SSE behavior in the sample-react app. Rapid disconnect/reconnect yields scrambled chunk order in the message pane.
anita: repro steps?
sam: open chat, then throttle network to offline for ~300ms then come back. UI sometimes shows piece 3 before piece 2.
kevin: likely buffering at a proxy or the client is reusing a cached stream. Any headers or ids in the payload?
sam: chat-lite events look like: `event: message
data: {"part":2, "text":"..."}` but part numbers are present. Still arrives out-of-order.
anita: could be reverse-proxy merging TCP segments from old connection with new one when keepalives overlap. We saw similar with nginx set to `proxy_buffering on` + low timeouts.
sam: quick curl test:
```
curl -sv -N -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  "https://api.redwood.dev/v1/stream/chat-lite?session=xyz"
```
kill the client then immediately rerun. You can see repeated `data:` sequences.
kevin: mitigation options:
- server: attach `seq` to each SSE `data` and emit `event: chunk_end id:<n>` markers per message so clients can reassemble
- client-sdk: support `dedupe` + `reorder` mode that buffers up to X ms for out-of-order seqs
- docs: recommend aborting previous stream before opening a new one, use jittered reconnects
anita: also add `Last-Event-ID` semantics for resume. But that needs server-side retention of last few events per session id. Not free for hosted.
sam: auth interplay: we saw 401 returned mid-stream after token refresh attempts. Client sometimes opens new connection with fresh token while old one still flushing -> duplicates.
kevin: for auth we could embed a short-lived `resume_token` in the initial SSE payload: `{ "resume_token":"abc123" }`. On reconnect client sends it as query param instead of full auth to tie to state.
anita: short-term DX fix: SDK should default to `auto_reconnect: true` with exponential backoff and `max_reconnect_burst: 1`. Also expose `maxReorderMS` and `dedupe` flags.
sam: agreed. I'll prototype a tiny JS helper for the sample app. Snippet for SDK docs: 
```js
// simple dedupe/reorder
let last = 0; const buf = new Map();
function onEvent(msg){
  const seq = msg.part;
  if(seq <= last) return; // drop duplicate/old
  buf.set(seq, msg);
  while(buf.has(last+1)){
    const next = buf.get(last+1);
    render(next.text);
    buf.delete(last+1);
    last += 1;
  }
  // if buf grows beyond threshold, flush oldest
  if(buf.size > 20) {
    // emit metric and drop
    metrics.increment('stream.buffer_overflow');
    buf.delete(Math.min(...buf.keys()));
  }
}
```
kevin: add a `stream.reorder` counter so we can see how frequent this is in hosted. Also record `resume_token` usage.
anita: infra note: we're rolling a proxy tweak tonight to reduce buffer window, should cut incidents in half. infra-bot: canary deploy scheduled 2026-04-02T03:00Z.
sam: I'll update the sample-app README with the curl repro, the JS snippet above, and a note to prefer `AbortController` to explicitly close streams before reconnect.
kevin: I'll file an SDK issue and a small PR for JS/TS exposing `maxReorderMS` and `dedupe=true` default for sample apps. Linking issue PR-4287 when created.
anita: long-term idea: consider switching sample apps to use WebSockets or gRPC for clients behind aggressive proxies. WebSockets have clearer framing and tend to survive weird keepalive behaviors.
sam: true but higher ops cost. doc update + SDK patch will help 90% of devs.
devex-bot: reminder: please attach PR links in this thread; pinned until resolved.
sam: thanks all, will post PRs once ready. :thumbsup:
